  "narrative": "There are no new evidence items to assess, so no status changes are required. However, the current active hypothesis queue is crowded with broad screens and low-prior marker interactions. Because the strongest current signals are feature_037 associated with stronger dependency, and feature_010/feature_002 associated with weaker dependency, the most scientifically urgent question is whether these strong binary predictors overlap or modify one another. I therefore defer the remaining broad binary/nominal screens (H25-H36) and the pre-specified log_PFS interactions for markers whose main effects were rejected (H37-H40) as investigation-only status changes. This keeps them available for later reconsideration but allows follow-up of the already-registered conditional contrasts H43-H53 to be prioritized. I also register one focused interaction refinement of the accepted feature_037 effect: the interaction contrast for feature_037=1 versus 0 within feature_010=1 relative to its complement. I register this as a positive-direction claim because the hypothesis is that the strong weaker-dependency association of feature_010 attenuates the stronger-dependency association of feature_037 among feature_010=1; that would produce a raw interaction favoring less negative/less stronger dependency in the feature_010=1 stratum. The alternatives are no modification or amplification of the feature_037 effect, which would later require a reversed interaction claim. All conclusions remain observational and limited to the supplied dataset; these comparisons do not establish independent causal effects.",
