  "narrative": "There are no due evidence assessments, so this stage focuses on new refinements that extend the current dataset-specific structure rather than repeating already established large effects. The dominant pattern is that feature_037=1 is strongly associated with much stronger dependency, while feature_010=1 and feature_002=1 are strongly associated with much weaker dependency. The most useful next questions are whether these associations persist in a clinically interpretable shorter/lower log_PFS stratum when the other dominant binary predictors are removed, whether feature_063 remains relevant when feature_037 or feature_002 are present, and whether the accepted feature_063 signal is separate from the near-threshold feature_003 candidate.\n\nThe first block of proposals tests the three dominant binary predictors in the lower half of fully observed log_PFS while conditioning on the other two dominant predictors. For feature_037 I claim a negative raw exposed-minus-comparator contrast because feature_037=1 was consistently associated with stronger dependency; the signed interval should be positive under direction -1. For feature_010 and feature_002 I claim positive raw contrasts because both were associated with weaker dependency. The alternatives are no threshold-exceeding association in this stratum, attenuation, or an opposite contrast. These are direct conditional effects rather than new interaction contrasts because the registered interactions were already small or opposite to the attenuation hypotheses; direct subgroup effects are more interpretable even if they may partly overlap with previously analyzed complements.\n\nThe second block refines the feature_063 family. H55 is now accepted in the triple-strong-absent stratum and independently replicated, so the next question is how broad that signal is. I propose feature_063 among feature_002=0 participants to complement the accepted feature_010=0 and feature_037=0 conditional contrasts. I also test feature_063 among feature_037=1 participants because feature_037 is the strongest predictor and may overshadow feature_063. Here I keep the claim direction as stronger dependency for feature_063 but anticipate uncertainty rather than a definite threshold effect, since feature_063 could be attenuated or masked among feature_037=1. I also test feature_037 within feature_063=1 to check whether the dominant feature_037 association remains enormous in that smaller stratum.\n\nThe final block separates feature_063 from feature_003 in the clean triple-strong-absent stratum. feature_003 has repeatedly near-threshold positive signed evidence under direction -1, but has not established a threshold-exceeding effect. Testing feature_003 with feature_063 absent asks whether its candidate signal is independent of the stronger feature_063 marker. Testing feature_063 with feature_003 absent asks whether the accepted feature_063 signal persists without the near-threshold predictor. If either fails, that is still informative: it would distinguish a robust feature_063 association from a broader or correlated dependency-score pattern. These are conditional observational contrasts only; persistence after additional conditioning does not imply causal independence, biological mechanism, or generalizability.\n\nI intentionally do not re-run active broad marginal screens H30-H36 or active direct overlap contrasts H47, H63, and H64 here. They remain useful for completing predictor coverage and the two-way overlap structure among the dominant binary predictors. The new proposals prioritize focused scientific questions that emerged after H55 validation: clinical stratum persistence, feature_063 hierarchy, and feature_003/feature_063 disentanglement.",
  "research_notes": "Current dataset-specific accepted core after H55 validation:\n- feature_037=1 is strongly associated with stronger dependency overall and in many conditional strata; validated and robust.\n- feature_010=1 and feature_002=1 are strongly associated with weaker dependency overall and in overlap/complement contrasts; interactions and upper-log_PFS attenuation claims are unsupported in this dataset.\n- feature_063=1 is accepted in triple-strong-absent stratum with independent validation, and remains accepted as conditional discovery evidence within feature_010=0. H51 remains unresolved because validation crossed threshold; marginal feature_063 not established.\n- feature_003 is a consistent near-threshold/subthreshold candidate but not accepted as threshold-exceeding.\n\nNew proposals registered this explore stage:\n1. Clean lower-PFS conditional main effects: feature_037 among feature_010=0/feature_002=0 and feature_040 <= median; feature_010 among feature_037=0/feature_002=0 and lower PFS; feature_002 among feature_037=0/feature_010=0 and lower PFS.\n2. Lower-PFS feature_063 in triple-strong-absent stratum.\n3. feature_063 mapping: feature_063 in feature_002=0; feature_063 in feature_037=1; feature_037 in feature_063=1.\n4. Clean feature_063/feature_003 disentanglement: feature_003 in triple absent + feature_063=0; feature_063 in triple absent + feature_003=0.\n\nPriority guidance for analysis: if slots are constrained, keep active H47, H63, H64 because they complete direct overlap structure; keep some broad marginal H30-H36; prioritize clean lower-PFS tests and feature_063 hierarchy tests over redundant large feature_037/010/002 contrasts. Avoid validating already robust large effects unless a new small threshold candidate emerges. All conclusions remain observational, dataset-specific, and conditional; they do not imply causality or biological mechanism."
