  "narrative": "The returned validations sharpen which claims can be carried forward and which must remain provisional. H15 is decisive and should be closed: feature_037=1 versus 0 shows a very large stronger-dependency association overall, with signed discovery estimate +0.804 [0.742,0.867] and independent validation estimate +0.800 [0.705,0.895]. The validation lower bound is far above the 0.15 threshold, so this is a robust dataset-specific association, not a marginal candidate. I still interpret it as observational association with the composite dependency score, not as a causal or mechanistic claim. H51 is not resolved in favor of acceptance. In the feature_037=0 subgroup, feature_063=1 versus 0 has discovery signed estimate +0.247 [0.151,0.342], but stringent independent validation gives +0.242 [0.109,0.376]. The direction is replicated, but the validation interval crosses the 0.15 threshold, so the broader conditional claim is not independently established. I therefore leave H51 unresolved and close the exact investigation because the targeted validation is the most direct evidence available for that exact claim. H73 also requires downgrading. Its discovery estimate was +0.280 [0.186,0.373] in the clean triple-strong-absent and feature_003=0 stratum, but validation gives +0.196 [0.072,0.320]. Again the sign and approximate direction are consistent, and the interval excludes null, but the lower bound is well below threshold under the stringent validation interval. The exact feature_063 claim conditional on feature_003 absence therefore remains unresolved, not accepted. I close the exact claim because further same-dataset contrasts would add multiplicity without directly resolving this validation-threshold uncertainty. The strongest supported structure remains: feature_037=1 is strongly associated with stronger dependency, and feature_010=1 and feature_002=1 are strongly associated with weaker dependency, with large validated or complement/overlap-supported effects and little support for the tested interactions or log_PFS attenuation claims. For feature_063, the cleanest claim remains the validated triple-strong-absent stratum H55. Conditional discovery evidence in feature_010=0 and feature_002=0 subgroups remains useful but near threshold and should not be read as a broad marginal effect. feature_003 remains a consistent near-threshold candidate but not accepted as threshold-exceeding. The most informative next analyses are the still-untested broad marginal screens and targeted complements of the accepted feature_063 conditional strata, including feature_063 among feature_010=1 and feature_002=1 participants. These tests will show whether feature_063 has a broader conditional structure or is mainly concentrated in clean absence-of-dominant-predictor strata.",
  "research_notes": "Final synthesis after H51, H15, and H73 validations:\n\nSupported core, observational and dataset-specific:\n- feature_037=1: robustly associated with much stronger dependency overall. H15 discovery +0.804 [0.742,0.867], validation +0.800 [0.705,0.895]. Accepted and exact overall investigation closed.\n- feature_010=1: associated with much weaker dependency overall and in complements/overlap conditionals. Large signed effects with lower bounds far above threshold. Negative-claim H13 was rejected as originally specified; directional H41/H47/H48/H63/H66 are the accepted representation.\n- feature_002=1: associated with much weaker dependency overall and in complements/overlap conditionals. Large signed effects with lower bounds far above threshold. Directional H42/H49/H50/H64/H67 accepted.\n- The dominant predictor pattern is broadly additive in the tested contrasts. Tested pairwise interactions among feature_037/010/002 and tested upper-half log_PFS attenuation interactions are unsupported.\n\nfeature_063:\n- Robust conditional validated claim: H55 in feature_037=0, feature_010=0, feature_002=0: discovery +0.252 [0.169,0.335], validation +0.281 [0.159,0.403]. Accepted. This should be presented as the main feature_063 claim, but only as a conditional association in a clean stratum.\n- H52 in feature_010=0 and H69 in feature_002=0 are accepted conditional discovery claims with lower bounds near threshold. Keep as supportive but weaker discovery-only conditional evidence, not broad marginal claims.\n- H51 in feature_037=0: discovery +0.247 [0.151,0.342], validation +0.242 [0.109,0.376]. Unresolved/closed because validation crossed threshold.\n- H73 in clean triple-absent and feature_003=0: discovery +0.280 [0.186,0.373], validation +0.196 [0.072,0.320]. Downgraded from accept to unresolved/closed because validation did not establish threshold exceedance.\n- Marginal feature_063 H21 remains unresolved/deferred; do not present marginal feature_063 as established.\n- H70 feature_063 within feature_037=1 remains unresolved; H68 lower-PFS clean stratum remains imprecise and unresolved.\n\nfeature_003:\n- Consistent near-threshold/subthreshold positive signed evidence across several strata, including H18, H53, H59, and H72, but no interval robustly excludes the 0.15 threshold. Treat as unresolved candidate, not accepted threshold effect.\n\nNext priorities:\n1. Run broad marginal screens H30-H36 if analysis slots allow, to complete predictor coverage.\n2. Test newly registered targeted complements for feature_063: feature_063 within feature_010=1 and within feature_002=1. These will map whether feature_063 persists in positive-dominant-predictor strata or mainly in absence strata.\n3. Do not spend further slots on large feature_037/010/002 overall contrasts; they are well characterized.\n4. Avoid accepting near-threshold feature_063 or feature_003 subgroup claims unless independent validation or much stronger discovery evidence is available.\n\nAll conclusions remain observational, dataset-specific, and conditional. They do not establish causality, biological mechanism, or generalizability."
