  "narrative": "This batch mostly corroborates the core dataset-specific marker pattern and finds no new decisive heterogeneity or broad-predictor effects. H118-H120 directly test whether the dominant marker associations persist within high constructed standardized-assay strata. In the high feature_038 stratum, feature_037 remains strongly associated with stronger composite dependency: +0.821 [0.687, 0.956], exposed n=102, comparator n=357. In the high feature_018 stratum, feature_010 remains strongly associated in the claimed weaker-dependency direction: +0.738 [0.603, 0.874], n=99/369. In the high feature_036 stratum, feature_002 also remains strongly associated: +0.806 [0.664, 0.948], n=91/386. All signed lower bounds are far above the 0.15-unit threshold and all cells satisfy the minimum requirement. I accept H118-H120 and close them as completed robustness probes; they do not create new independent discoveries beyond the already accepted marginal marker pattern, but they make it less likely that the core associations are confined to one simple stratum.\n\nH115 is the most useful new result. It estimates feature_027=1 versus 0 in the stricter clean stratum excluding feature_037, feature_010, feature_002, feature_063, and feature_003. The signed estimate is +0.747 [0.688, 0.806] with exposed n=45 and comparator n=668. The interval lower bound is far above threshold and the exposed cell is adequate, so I accept the claim as a dataset-specific conditional association. Because this comparison specifically addresses whether the accepted feature_027 association is merely a proxy for the bounded feature_063 context or the near-threshold feature_003 predictor, I request independent validation. H115 remains active pending that validation.\n\nH121 estimates feature_027 in the high feature_030 half and is also threshold-exceeding: +0.775 [0.661, 0.890] with n=130/871. However, H122 shows the corresponding low feature_030 comparison is not estimable because there are zero exposed feature_027=1 observations in that half. Therefore H121 should be interpreted as a conditional association observed among high feature_030 participants and as evidence that all feature_027 exposed observations occur in the high feature_030 stratum; it is not a demonstrated median-split effect across the full feature_030 range. I accept H121 as completed conditional corroboration and close it, but I do not elevate it into a precise clinical-course or feature_030-dependent claim. H122 remains unresolved and closed because the requested low-stratum comparison had insufficient exposed observations and provides no usable evidence either way.\n\nThe new broad and interaction probes do not support threshold-exceeding associations. H117, the feature_037-by-feature_024 interaction, gives +0.174 [0.035, 0.312]. The point estimate exceeds the threshold, but the lower bound does not, so the evidence is not decisive for a scientifically meaningful interaction. Given the multiplicity of interaction probes, I reject and close it as lack of evidence for the claimed heterogeneity, not as proof of additivity. H123, feature_062 level_001 versus level_003, is +0.093 [-0.009, 0.196] and is rejected. The feature_037 and feature_010 interactions by feature_062 level_003 are also not supported: H124 gives -0.059 [-0.194, 0.076] and H125 gives +0.040 [-0.097, 0.177]. The median-split interactions H126 and H127 similarly fail the lower-bound threshold: H126 gives +0.072 [-0.052, 0.196] and H127 gives +0.019 [-0.106, 0.143]. I reject and close H123-H127. These are dataset-specific negative probes; they do not establish that no interaction or association exists, only that these tested contrasts do not provide evidence for threshold-exceeding effects. All accepted claims remain observational associations within the supplied dataset, without causal interpretation or assumed generalizability.",
