  "narrative": "This batch sharply clarifies the status of the two borderline predictors. For feature_003, every strict clean context now probes the same small signed signal: the point estimates are positive in the claimed direction (feature_003=1 associated with a more negative, stronger composite-dependency score) but typically only around 0.13-0.20. The 95% Welch lower bounds are consistently below the 0.15 threshold: upper feature_040 +0.171 [0.093,0.249] (H138), lower feature_040 +0.161 [0.076,0.246] (H139), high feature_008 +0.187 [0.094,0.281] (H141), low feature_008 +0.153 [0.080,0.226] (H142), high feature_030 +0.197 [0.119,0.275] (H144), and low feature_030 +0.130 [0.046,0.214] (H145). The feature_003-by-feature_008 interaction H143 is +0.034 [-0.084,0.152], failing threshold heterogeneity, so I reject that interaction as not supported, not as proof of strict additivity. Because many intervals span the threshold and some point estimates are below it, no exact feature_003 context should be accepted; feature_003 remains an unresolved borderline predictor, and I close these exact-context investigations rather than continue threshold-chasing in multiple stress strata.\n\nFor feature_063, the batch supports bounded, exact-context associations rather than a broad predictor effect. The high feature_008 clean context H140 is +0.251 [0.134,0.368], just below threshold by lower bound, and the high feature_030 clean context H147 is +0.278 [0.141,0.415], also below threshold. The complementary low feature_030 clean context H148 is +0.290 [0.174,0.407] with adequate cells, so I accept H148 as a dataset-specific exact-context association. The low feature_008 clean context H146 is the strongest new direct result: +0.311 [0.182,0.441] with 56 exposed and 338 comparator observations. Although the discovery interval exceeds the threshold, feature_063 has repeatedly attenuated under independent validation or broader contexts, and this claim is near-threshold after many probe